Subject: gpu: Check GL errors before marking WebGPU Skia-fallback images
 cleared

When WebGPU uses the Skia fallback with Ganesh-GL, Skia does not surface
GL driver errors from uploads or clears. Drain GL errors before writing
to an uncleared shared image in UploadContentsToSkia and
ClearSharedImageWithSkia, and only mark it cleared if none were raised.

Bug: 566384898
Change-Id: I9df266e7198cadca53759dca49edc15ae9574889
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8520144
Reviewed-by: Kai Ninomiya <kainino@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Jonathan Ross <jonross@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1717684}

Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y): context-only conflict. The 3-way
merge pulled the unrelated kAllowedMailboxBufferUsages constant into
the ShouldCheckGLErrors() hunk as context; it was not taken. The
include ordering differs because this branch has no
dawn_wire_server.h include. All functional hunks applied verbatim.

